{"url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/departments/mechanical-engineering/graduate-programs", "final_url": "https://umdearborn.edu/cecs/departments/mechanical-engineering/graduate-programs", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-14", "text": "Skip to main content\nEnter your keywords\nSearchsearch\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nDepartments\nResearch\nIndustry & Community\nLife at CECS\nAlumni & Friends\nAbout\nUM-Dearborn Home\nStudent One-Stop\nFaculty & Staff\nCommunity & Business\nAlumni\nApply\nGiving\nBrowse A-Z\nBreadcrumb\nHome College of Engineering and Computer Science Departments Mechanical Engineering Graduate Programs\nIN THIS SECTION\nMechanical Engineering\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nOur Faculty & Research\nToggle Submenu\nLaboratories\nGraduate Programs\nEngineering Real-World Solutions\nThe Mechanical Engineering department offers nationally ranked master's and doctoral programs, combining academic rigor with interdisciplinary breadth and practical applications. Students benefit from expert faculty, strong industry ties, and excellent facilities. The programs are continuously updated to provide the latest technological knowledge and skills, ensuring graduates are competitive globally.\nOur master\u2019s programs feature evening and online classes and cater to both full-time and part-time students. The doctoral education includes a full-time, fully funded PhD program for high-level research and a part-time industry-based Doctor of Engineering (Dr. Eng.) program.\nApply Now\nRequest Information\nVisit Campus\nMSE in Automotive and Mobility Systems Engineering\nMSE in Mechanical Engineering\nMSE in Bioengineering\nMSE in Materials Science and Engineering\nPh.D. in Mechanical Sciences and Engineering\nD.Eng. in Automotive Systems and Mobility\nAccelerated Master's Programs\nOur Ph.D. Students\nGraduate Advising\nFor additional academic information or to schedule an advising appointment, please contact:\nMecha